[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/2680651632","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740#issuecomment-2680651632","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740","id":2680651632,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM6fx39w","user":{"login":"ximatest","id":77187370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTg3Mzcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77187370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest","html_url":"https://github.com/ximatest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ximatest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-25T05:41:27Z","updated_at":"2025-02-25T05:41:27Z","body":"When associating a client with an nf_instance, the reference count (REF) is incremented twice during the process. However, when releasing the nf_instance, REF is decremented only once. This asymmetry might be the root cause of the issue. \n@acetcom Could you please review this? Thank you!\n\n\nogs_sbi_client_t *ogs_sbi_client_add(\n        OpenAPI_uri_scheme_e scheme,\n        char *fqdn, uint16_t fqdn_port,\n        ogs_sockaddr_t *addr, ogs_sockaddr_t *addr6)\n{\n    ...\n    ogs_debug(\"ogs_sbi_client_add [%s]\", OpenAPI_uri_scheme_ToString(scheme));\n    OGS_OBJECT_REF(client);\n\t....\n}\n\nvoid ogs_sbi_client_associate(ogs_sbi_nf_instance_t *nf_instance)\n{\n    ogs_sbi_client_t *client = NULL;\n\n    ogs_assert(nf_instance);\n\n    client = nf_instance_find_client(nf_instance);//Here, OGS_OBJECT_REF is called once.\n    ogs_assert(client);\n\n    ogs_debug(\"[%s] NFInstance associated [%s]\",\n            nf_instance->nf_type ?\n                OpenAPI_nf_type_ToString(nf_instance->nf_type) : \"NULL\",\n            nf_instance->id);\n\n    OGS_SBI_SETUP_CLIENT(nf_instance, client);//hen, OGS_OBJECT_REF is called again elsewhere.\n\n    nf_service_associate_client_all(nf_instance);\n}\n\n\nvoid ogs_sbi_nf_instance_remove(ogs_sbi_nf_instance_t *nf_instance)\n{\n    ...\n    if (nf_instance->client)\n        ogs_sbi_client_remove(nf_instance->client);\n    \n    ogs_pool_free(&nf_instance_pool, nf_instance);\n}\n\nvoid ogs_sbi_client_remove(ogs_sbi_client_t *client)\n{\n    ...\n\n    /* ogs_sbi_client_t is always created with reference context */\n    if (OGS_OBJECT_IS_REF(client)) {\n        OGS_OBJECT_UNREF(client);//But during cleanup, only one OGS_OBJECT_UNREF is invoked.\"\n        return;\n    }\n\n    ogs_debug(\"CLEINT removed [%d]\", client->reference_count);\n\n    ...\n}","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/2680651632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/2696268777","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740#issuecomment-2696268777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740","id":2696268777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM6gtcvp","user":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T05:36:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T05:36:35Z","body":"@ximatest \n\nI’ve addressed this issue you raised regarding incomplete NF instance cleanup and the fallback to the default port 80. The fix comprises two parts:\n\nWe now send a GOAWAY frame to all active sessions on server shutdown to prevent RST errors when curl 8.9.1 reuses connections after an NF restart.\nAlthough the reference count behavior was originally intended, we found that the nf_instance pointer was not fully released during cleanup. We resolved this by switching to storing the nf_instance_id and verifying instance validity during recovery, ensuring that the proper client is used.\n\nThese changes have been merged into the main branch. Thank you for bringing this to our attention!\n\nSukchan Lee","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/2696268777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/2713084882","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740#issuecomment-2713084882","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/3740","id":2713084882,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM6htmPS","u